; Stage 0 — ROUND 11: ONE site rule, on the canonical logical form only.
;
; Austin's round-11 ruling: logical rules are named by SHAPES; N and T are
; layout descriptions and never appear at this stratum. Every recorded
; spelling reaches the canonical form through the three canonicalization
; rewrites (cublaslt_marker_canonicalize.egg), so the round-10 per-spelling
; site rules (the "A[m,k],B[n,k]" folded-permute rule and the sandwich-
; sibling rule) are DELETED: their spellings now arrive here already
; canonicalized, with non-canonically-stored operands presented as rank-2
; transpose VIEWS.
;
; The rule mints the SAME site term and NOTHING else — no layout data, no
; orientation, no bounds guards. Multiple readings per site are legal
; multiplicity (descriptor TERMS coexist; election picks; the k=1,n=1 weld
; corner double-reads soundly — both readings of a [1,1] operand describe
; the same matrix).
;
; Guards are LOGICAL-shape unification (R5): ?m ?n ?k bound ONCE across
; operand storage shapes, product shape, and out shape. The sliced-source
; attack (storage k=7, product k=3) still dies here.
;
; Anchor: the LogicalReduceSum (no independently quantified atoms).
; Product-space convention: ShapeLit lists outermost-first; CoordVar /
; ReduceSum axes count from the END (axis 0 = innermost). Product is
; [m, n, k] with k the reduced innermost axis.
;
; Site admission is UNGUARDED — logical identity only. Symbolic-extent
; refusal is NOT this rule's job: the descriptor stratum's literal-extent
; gate keeps symbolic sites from ever assembling an op.
; ============================================================================
; --- THE canonical form: A[m,k] (map c2 c0), B[k,n] (map c0 c1) ------------
(rule
  (
    (= ?out (LogicalReduceSum ?prod 0))
    (= ?prod (LogicalMul ?a_bcast ?b_bcast))
    (= ?a_bcast (LogicalIndexMapApply ?a ?a_map ?prod_shape))
    (= ?b_bcast (LogicalIndexMapApply ?b ?b_map ?prod_shape))
    (= ?a_map (IndexMapLit
        (IntExprCons (CoordVar ?prod_shape 2)
          (IntExprCons (CoordVar ?prod_shape 0) (IntExprNil)))
        ?a_shape))
    (= ?b_map (IndexMapLit
        (IntExprCons (CoordVar ?prod_shape 0)
          (IntExprCons (CoordVar ?prod_shape 1) (IntExprNil)))
        ?b_shape))
    (= ?prod_shape (ShapeLit
        (IntExprCons ?m (IntExprCons ?n (IntExprCons ?k (IntExprNil))))))
    (= (shape-of ?a) ?a_shape)
    (= ?a_shape (ShapeLit (IntExprCons ?m (IntExprCons ?k (IntExprNil)))))
    (= (shape-of ?b) ?b_shape)
    (= ?b_shape (ShapeLit (IntExprCons ?k (IntExprCons ?n (IntExprNil)))))
    (= (shape-of ?out) (ShapeLit (IntExprCons ?m (IntExprCons ?n (IntExprNil)))))
    (= (dtype-of ?a) (F32))
    (= (dtype-of ?b) (F32))
    (= (dtype-of ?out) (F32))
  )
  ((let ?site (CublasLtLogicalMatmulSite ?a ?b ?out)))
)
; ============================================================================
